.PP
\fBskill\fR matches procps-ng's behaviour on the supported flag set —
selector logic, signal parsing, exit codes, and the \fB\-l\fR /
\fB\-L\fR signal-listing format. Some procps-ng features are not yet
implemented:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-i\fR (interactive), \fB\-f\fR (fast), and \fB\-w\fR (warnings)
mode flags.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-ns\fR \fIPID\fR and \fB\-\-nslist\fR \fINS\fR\fB,...\fR —
namespace-based selection.
.IP \(bu 2
Real-time signals (\fBSIGRTMIN\fR..\fBSIGRTMAX\fR) cannot be named;
they are still deliverable by number via \fB\-\-signal\fR \fIN\fR.
.PP
Error messages for invalid arguments use different wording.
